On 7/24/05, GREGORY DYKE <gregory.dyke@epfl.ch> wrote:
> The "parts of sentence" are all the rules of the grammar (of which there
> are a fairly large number) "parts of speech" are the various selma'o
> augmented by the _selma'o be zi'o_ which are CMENE and GISMU. 

CMENE and BRIVLA. 

{gerku}, {jungau}, {.iglu} and {cidjrspageti} are all the same "part of speech"
BRIVLA.

GISMU, LUJVO and FUhIVLA are not really full parts of speech on their own,
but morphological subclasses of BRIVLA. They only differ in their form, not
in how they are used.

Also, selmaho GOhA is almost the same part of speech as BRIVLA.

